      about: "PM compliance is the share of preventive jobs done when they were due. The grace window, 10% of the interval, is a common convention, not a standard: a weekly PM may be up to 16.8 hours late, a monthly one 3 days. Each PM is created one interval before it is due, so DATEDIFF of created and due is the interval. Conveyor 3's 20 October PM was done two days late; Hoop Driver 1's 3 November PM was never done, and a missing done_ts fails the comparison, so it counts as missed. 86.7% overall. PMs are done in the breaks between paid time in this sample, so they do not reduce the 9,450 planned minutes. The work orders, hours and their dates are illustrative; the faults are the canonical fault_log.",
