      about: "Reactive work is done when something breaks, on the machine's schedule; planned work on yours. Half the crew's hours went to breakdowns this week. A planned share of around 80% is a widely quoted benchmark for mature maintenance, not a standard, but 50% says the crew is mostly firefighting. SUM(SUM(act_hours)) OVER () is the total of the grouped sums, so each row can show its share in one query. The work orders, hours and their dates are illustrative; the faults are the canonical fault_log.",
