      about: "Backlog in hours means little on its own; backlog in crew-weeks says how long the open work would take with the time the crew actually has for these machines. 12 hours a week is an illustrative share of the crew's time. 27 hours is 2.25 weeks, inside the 2 to 4 weeks often quoted as healthy: much less and the crew may run out of planned work, much more and jobs wait too long. The number only means something if the estimates are honest.",
